"""
emed_authored.py - authored repairs for EMED questions the scan destroyed.
==========================================================================

Three groups, all keyed by (bank, index-in-the-merged-bank):

  * 92 HOLLOW stems. The vignette lived entirely inside a scanned image that
    OCR could not read, so all that survived was the lead-in ("Which one of the
    following is the most likely diagnosis?"). Each vignette is REWRITTEN from
    that question's own explanation and option list, with the findings the
    original showed as a picture stated in words instead. Australian units and
    settings throughout.

  * 17 BROKEN questions where the scan destroyed the option that happened to be
    the correct answer ("C) Eco" for ECG, "B) Of" for orf, "A) Om" for
    progressive supranuclear palsy).

  * 17 QUARANTINED questions, mostly calculation items whose numeric options
    were shredded. The explanations work through the arithmetic, so the answer
    is recoverable even when the option list is not.

Where the OCR'd answer LETTER contradicts the question's own explanation, the
explanation wins - the same failure mode ANSWER_OVERRIDES already corrects.

Applied at load time by emed_clean.clean_banks(), BEFORE the hollow/blank check,
so these questions stop being unservable and are no longer dropped.

Fields per entry (all optional):
    stem          full replacement question_text
    stem_replace  (old, new) substring swap, for surgical edits
    options       full replacement option list
    answer        correct_answer_letter
    explanation   full replacement explanation
"""

